  },
  "paragraphs": [
    {
      "num": "01",
      "en": "Taking {responsibility} for mistakes is a {positive} step, but don't {beat} yourself up about them or leave yourself at the {bottom} of an emotional well.To {err} is human.Mistakes aren't {bombs} that {explode} in your life to ruin everythingIt's just as {important} to show yourself some {forgiveness} .You can use the following writing {exercise} to help you {bounce} back and soar ( (高飞) ) once again.",
      "cn": "对错误负 责 是 积极的 一步，但不要为此 过分自责 ，也不要让自己陷入情绪的谷 底 。 犯错 是人之常情。错误不是在生活中 爆炸 并毁掉一切的 炸弹 。 宽恕 自己同样 重要 。你可以通过以下的写作 练习 来帮助自己重新 振作 ，再次展翅高飞。"
    },
    {
      "num": "02",
      "en": "In a journal or on a {sheet} of paper, put the {title} \" {Personal} strengths.\"Imagine you're a {candidate} applying for your dream job.You would highlight your skills and achievements to impress the {boss} .Now list all the {characteristics} you like about yourself.Are you {caring} ? {Creative} ? {Generous} ? A good {listener} ? Give them a {nod} of approval.They don't have to be world-changing, or as great as mastering {calligraphy} , speaking {French} , or playing the {jazz} guitar, just {aspects} of your {personality} that you're {proud} of.",
      "cn": "在日记中或一 张 纸上，写下 标题 \" 个人 优势\"。想象一下，你是一名正在申请理想工作的 求职者 。你会着重突出你的技能和成就，来给 老板 留下深刻印象。现在列出你所喜欢的自己的所有 特质 。你 乐于助人 吗？ 有创造力 吗？ 慷慨大方 吗？是一个好的 倾听者 吗？认可这些特质就 点点头 吧。它们不必是能改变世界的，也不必像精通 书法 、会说 法语 或弹奏 爵士 吉他那样厉害，只要是你 个性 中能让你引以为 豪 的 方面 都可以。"
    },
    {
      "num": "03",
      "en": "At the top of a second page, put the heading \"Acts of {kindness} .\"On this one, list all the positive things you've done for others.It might be the time when you helped a {classmate} with his {homework} and offered him your {coat} on a cold {November} night, when you did the {ironing} without being asked, or when you {baked cookies} after the family had had a {tiring} day.It doesn't have to go so far as volunteering at a {church} or {praying} daily. {Whatever} it is, no matter how small it might seem, write it down.",
      "cn": "在第二页的顶部，写下标题\" 善 举\"。在这一页，列出你为他人做过的所有积极的事情。可能是你在 11月 的一个寒冷夜晚帮一位 同学 完成 家庭作业 ，并把自己的 外套 借给他的时候；可能是在没有被要求的情况下主动 熨 了衣服；也可能是在家人度过 疲惫的 一天后，为他们 烤 了 饼干 。不一定非要做到像去 教堂 做义工或每天 祈祷 那种程度。 不管 是 什么 事情，不管它看起来多么微不足道，都要把它写下来。"
    },
    {
      "num": "04",
      "en": "You could ask a friend or family member to help {add} to your list.Whether they're a student in a {dormitory} or a professional working {downstairs} in a {studio} , they might like to have a go at doing the exercise, too.That way, you could {exchange} thoughts on what makes {each} of you {special} and the aspects of your personality that {shine} through.This process will make you both the teacher and the {pupil} , guiding yourself towards growth.In fact, don't wait until you've made a mistake to try this—it's a great way to boost {self-confidence} , which will act like {wings} that lift you into the sky.",
      "cn": "你可以请朋友或家人帮你 补充 这个列表。无论他们是 宿舍 里的学生，还是在 楼下工作室 工作的专业人士，他们或许也乐意尝试这个练习。这样一来，你们就可以 交流 想法了，探讨 每个 人的 独特 之处，以及你们身上那些 闪光 点。这个过程会让你既是老师又是 学生 ，引导自己不断成长。事实上，不要等到犯了错误才去尝试这样做——这是增强 自信 的一个好方法，而自信就像把你送上天空的 翅膀 。"
    },
    {
      "num": "05",
      "en": "It's something of a cliché ( (陈词滥调) ) that most people learn not from their {successes} but their mistakes.The thing is, it's true.But don't {punish} yourself by pressing your disappointment so hard on your {chest} .Whatever the mistake, remember it isn't a {fixed} aspect of your personality.Life can be like a game of {bowling} : sometimes you {knock} down all the pins, and other times you face a split.We're all changing and learning all the time, and mistakes are a positive way to develop and {grow} .",
      "cn": "大多数人并非从 成功 中学习，而是从错误中学习，这种论调有些老套。事实的确如此。但是，不要把失望重重压在 胸膛 来 惩罚 自己。无论犯了什么错误，都要记住，它不是你个性中 固定不变的 一面。生活就像一场 保龄球 比赛：有时你能 击 倒所有木瓶，有时却会面临球瓶分散的困境。我们都在不断改变和学习，而错误正是促进我们发展和 成长 的一种积极方式。 5NoOncib/NjiX02BpMIzP+Fxyt/ox+WDCb+dhfH7KaYaJ4u5RsVmLondVmcHiLum9J1BQErGzJvzqa5GEIz4ZA=="
    }
  ],
